\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces The SiliQun software architecture. This modular framework is divided into four distinct layers: a flexible numerical backend (supporting NumPy and CuPy), a dual simulation core featuring both an MPS engine for 1D chains and a GPU state vector engine for 2D grids, a dedicated physics engine containing calibrated device profiles and noise models, and an uppermost layer that provides a Gymnasium-compatible RL environment.}}{4}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:architecture}{{1}{4}{The SiliQun software architecture. This modular framework is divided into four distinct layers: a flexible numerical backend (supporting NumPy and CuPy), a dual simulation core featuring both an MPS engine for 1D chains and a GPU state vector engine for 2D grids, a dedicated physics engine containing calibrated device profiles and noise models, and an uppermost layer that provides a Gymnasium-compatible RL environment}{figure.1}{}}
